CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --verbosity 9
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
object bits: [0-9]* addressed objects need
--
too many addressed objects
--
The disallowed pattern is the point. This program addresses 300 distinct
globals, more than the 256 that ansi_c.default_object_bits allows, so before
object_bits was sized to the program it died in bv_pointerst::add_addr with
"too many addressed objects" and produced no verdict -- after paying for symex
and the concurrency encoding.

The required "object bits:" line checks the sizing actually fired rather than
the test passing because the program happened to stay under the default.

test.pl matches with grep, so these are basic regular expressions: no '+'
or '{n,m}'.
